  "caption": "Quinn tried yoga and discovered the toes are unreachable. Theory: arms are too short.\n\nTouching your toes depends on more than hamstring length: hip hinge, spine and how well your nervous system tolerates the stretch all play a part. Plenty of fit, healthy people can't do it, and that's often fine.\n\nIf you do want more range: build strength through a long range with slow hip hinges, hold stretches for 30–60 seconds most days (strong stretch, not pain), warm up before testing yourself, and give it 4–8 weeks. Before sport, dynamic moves suit better than long holds.\n\nTingling down the leg while stretching, or a sudden loss of flexibility on one side, is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
